From 9bfcd4c43750f052330ced0308b31bcb2ea9e1f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Choque <luis.choque.castro@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:07:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(security): close stored XSS in markdown, changelogs
 and comments

- markdownToHTML() now returns HTML sanitized with DOMPurify (already
  loaded by the layout); <style>, form controls and style attributes are
  also dropped. Every markdown innerHTML (mod and build descriptions,
  upload and edit previews) goes through it. Without DOMPurify it fails
  closed and shows the markdown as escaped text.
- Build changelogs are rendered with | escape instead of | safe.
- Comments are built with DOM nodes (comments.js): message, user names
  and URLs are set through textContent or validated attributes, never
  concatenated into HTML; inline onclick handlers are gone.
- Mod cards (profile, featured, build upload preview) escape every field
  (name, short description, version, user, image URL) with the shared
  escapeHTML helper. The profile lists unapproved mods, so an unreviewed
  short description could run script for any visitor, moderators
  included.
- showError/showSuccess and the upload toasts escape their message.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
